<title>UK: Geest signs food deal with Albert Heijn.</title>
<headline>Geest signs food deal with Albert Heijn.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Geest Plc said on Monday it has agreed with Albert Heijn, the subsidiary of Dutch supermarket group Royal Ahold, to manufacture a new chilled food range for Heijn in the UK and Belgium.</p>
<p>It said that it will buy the Belgian manufacturing company Vaco B.V. from Ahold for 4.9 million stg in cash.  </p>
<p>Food group Geest said this was the first substantial partnership with a European retailer that it has entered into and Vaco would be the first Geest prepared foods facility outside the UK.</p>
<p>It said Albert Heijn had a 27 percent share of the Dutch grocery trade with 646 supermarkets and annualised sales of 4.0 billion stg in total.</p>
<p>By 1228 GMT, shares in Geest has climbed 7-1/2p to 255p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
